<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1156">1156</a>–<a href="/years/1222">1222</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Raymond VI was count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a> from 1194 to 1222. Accused of protecting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catharism">Cathars</a>, he was excommunicated, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/albigensian-crusade">Albigensian Crusade</a> from 1209 brought northern French armies under Simon de Montfort into his lands. He was defeated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-ii-of-aragon">Peter II of Aragon</a> at Muret in 1213 and lost Toulouse, but recovered it in 1217 and held it until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raymond-vi-count-of-toulouse.jpg" alt="Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raimond6Toulouse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The heaviest blows came during the Albigensian Crusade, when Simon de Montfort defeated <b>Raymond VI</b> and Peter II of Aragon at the Battle of Muret in 1213.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">County of Toulouse · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Count Bernard IV joined <b>Raymond VI of Toulouse</b> against the crusaders and was present at the battle of Muret in 1213, where Peter II of Aragon was killed.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-comminges">County of Comminges</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Saint-Gilles, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/france">France</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=43.68,4.43&amp;year=1198" aria-label="Saint-Gilles on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4656 616 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Raymond VI, Count of Toulouse"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5106 886h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5106 886h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=43.68,4.43&amp;year=1198">What was here in 1198? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
